# Environment Configuration Template for phone2tg-proxy
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# How the app reads this file:
#   * A `.env` file in the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY is parsed into the app
#     config (go-core-fx/config -> koanf). `.env` is gitignored - never commit
#     a real one.
#   * Real environment variables are applied AFTER the file, so they win when
#     both define the same key.
#   * Key names are lowercased and nested with a double underscore by the
#     loader: HTTP__OPENAPI__ENABLED -> http.openapi.enabled. The uppercase
#     form below is the project convention.
#   * Every key in the HTTP / TELEGRAM / REDIS / STORAGE / I18N sections maps
#     1:1 to a leaf in internal/config/config.go. An omitted key falls back to
#     the default shown here.
#   * The bot always runs in polling mode - there is no variable for it.

# =============================================================================
# HTTP SERVER CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# HTTP Listen Address
# Purpose: Address the Fiber HTTP server binds to. Bind 0.0.0.0 in Docker or
#   behind a load balancer, otherwise the published port is unreachable from
#   outside the container or host.
# Format: host:port
# Default: 127.0.0.1:3000
# Example: 0.0.0.0:3000
HTTP__ADDRESS=127.0.0.1:3000

# Trusted Proxy Header
# Purpose: Header the server reads the client IP from when the request comes
#   from a proxy listed in HTTP__PROXIES.
# Format: HTTP header name
# Default: X-Forwarded-For
# Example: X-Real-IP
HTTP__PROXY_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For

# Trusted Proxies
# Purpose: Proxy IP addresses or CIDR ranges whose forwarded client IP is
#   accepted. Requests from any other client keep their real remote address.
# Format: JSON array of IP addresses or CIDR ranges. A comma-separated list
#   is NOT parsed - it arrives as one malformed entry.
# Default: [] (no proxy is trusted)
# Example: ["10.0.0.1","10.0.0.2"]
# Example: ["10.0.0.0/8"]
HTTP__PROXIES=[]

# =============================================================================
# OPENAPI DOCUMENTATION CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Serve the OpenAPI Document
# Purpose: Serves the Swagger UI and the OpenAPI JSON under /api/v1/docs.
#   Set it to false to remove the documentation endpoints.
# Format: Boolean (true|false)
# Default: true
# Example: false
HTTP__OPENAPI__ENABLED=true

# Public Host of the Served Specification
# Purpose: Host written into the served OpenAPI spec. Empty means the host is
#   taken from the first incoming request.
# Format: Host name without scheme
# Default: (empty - taken from the request)
# Example: api.example.com
HTTP__OPENAPI__PUBLIC_HOST=

# Public Base Path of the Served Specification
# Purpose: Base path written into the served OpenAPI spec. Empty keeps the
#   /api/v1 path baked into the generated spec.
# Format: Absolute path
# Default: (empty - keeps /api/v1)
# Example: /openapi
HTTP__OPENAPI__PUBLIC_PATH=

# =============================================================================
# TELEGRAM BOT CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Telegram Bot Token
# Purpose: Token of the Telegram bot created with @BotFather. The app refuses
#   to start without a well-formed token.
# Format: <numeric bot id>:<35 word characters>
# Default: (none - required)
# Example: 123456789:AAHfakeTokenForExampleOnly000000000
TELEGRAM__TOKEN=

# Telegram Proxy URL
# Purpose: SOCKS5 proxy used for outgoing Telegram API calls. Only socks5://
#   and socks5h:// are accepted and the URL is validated at startup. The
#   HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY variables are NOT honoured.
# Format: socks5://[user:password@]host:port
# Default: (empty - direct connection)
# Example: socks5://127.0.0.1:1080
# Example: socks5h://user:password@127.0.0.1:1080
TELEGRAM__PROXY_URL=

# Telegram Request Timeout
# Purpose: Bounds every outgoing Telegram API request end to end - dialing the
#   SOCKS5 proxy (including the handshake), TLS, and reading the response
#   share one deadline. A request over the bound fails fast and is retried by
#   the polling loop instead of hanging the bot. Must stay above the 8s
#   getUpdates long-poll hold, or every polling cycle aborts.
# Format: Go duration (30s, 1m, ...)
# Default: 30s
# Example: 30s
TELEGRAM__TIMEOUT=30s

# =============================================================================
# REDIS CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Redis Connection URL
# Purpose: Redis instance holding the phone number to Telegram ID mapping. The
#   app pings Redis on startup and fails to start when it is unreachable.
# Format: redis:// or rediss:// connection URL
# Default: redis://localhost:6379/0
# Example: redis://user:password@redis.example.com:6379/0
# Example: rediss://redis.example.com:6379/0
REDIS__URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# =============================================================================
# STORAGE CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Phone Number Hashing Secret
# Purpose: HMAC-SHA256 key used to hash phone numbers before they are stored
#   in Redis. Changing it invalidates every phone number already stored. An
#   empty value only logs a warning and hashes with an empty key.
# Format: Arbitrary string
# Default: (empty - set a real value for production)
# Example: change-me-to-a-long-random-string
STORAGE__SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# INTERNATIONALIZATION CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Default Language
# Purpose: Language used when no translation matches the requested one. The
#   file <translations path>/<language>.json must exist or the app fails to
#   start.
# Format: File stem of a translation file (en, ru)
# Default: en
# Example: ru
I18N__DEFAULT_LANGUAGE=en

# Translations Path
# Purpose: Directory the i18n JSON translation files are loaded from. Relative
#   paths are resolved against the working directory.
# Format: File path
# Default: i18n/locales
# Example: /app/i18n/locales
I18N__TRANSLATIONS_PATH=i18n/locales

# =============================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT CONFIGURATION
# =============================================================================

# Debug Logging
# Purpose: Switches the logger from the production JSON configuration to the
#   development (human-readable, colored) one. `make air` sets it.
# Note: The logger reads this from the PROCESS ENVIRONMENT - the .env file is
#   only parsed into the app config and is not exported into the environment.
#   Export it in the shell (DEBUG=1 go run .) instead of setting it here.
# Format: Boolean (true|false) - "1" also counts as true
# Default: false
# Example: 1
# DEBUG=1
